Manners.; Mos.
Mannered. Moral.; Moratus.
See <Moral>.

@AC 788[2]. For the manners and faces are the types of the interiors.

@822[2]. Those who are more polite... first salute each other... and then go behind and strike...

@1215[end]. Here, the things which belong to morals or life have the precedence.

@2590. The Gentiles who have led a moral life...

@3179[end]. The custom of writing thus... @4442. @8891[4]. @9942[4]. Compare @HH 323[end].

@4145[3]. In marriage love, the good which precedes and initiates is beauty, or agreement of manners, or...

@5127. "According to the former manner" (Genesis 40:13) = from the law of order. Explained.

@6495[2]. He appears actually moral and civil... But this plane is nothing in the other life.

@DP 298[2]. The good (then) become still wiser and more moral.

@CL 33[2]. (The sexes) differ also in gestures and manners.

@79[7]. Take care not to speak anything against good manners.

@90[3]. The manners (of the male) all partake of the predominance of the understanding; whence it is that the acts of his life, which are meant by the manners, are rational...

@91. But that the female is born to be voluntary... may also be evident from her... manners.

@218. (This is evident) from the manners, in that with men they are more unrestrained; but with women more elegant.

@246. That the first of the external causes of cold is unlikeness of lower minds and of manners. Explained. Defined.

@330. They agreed that women have also... a spiritual beauty, which is that of the love and manners... In the Spiritual World the beauty is the form of the love and manners...

@--[2]. Every woman wants to... appear beautiful in manners.

@331. Every wife loves her husband... from his intelligence in his office and conduct.

@405. The spiritual love their children... from their virtues and good conduct. @--[2].

@SE 4396. Those who had been (only) externally well behaved.

@5353. Who had lived morally -morate-.

@5354. Had led a moral life, but not from doctrine...

@DWis 10. 3. 2. According to the manner.

