@1053[2]. There is another kind of profanation of holy things with those who have... the holy things of the Word, of the Church, and of worship, as means. It is according to Divine order that... domination be the means to promote the end; for when holy things are the end, and domination is the means, the Lord is worshipped... But when... holy things are the means, man is worshipped in the Lord's place. For means regard the end as servants their lord; and the end regards the means as a lord his servants.

@--[3]. And the end conjoins the means with itself, so that they are as a one.

@1086[5]. For when the Lord operates, He does not operate from primes through middle things into ultimates; but from primes through ultimates, and so into middle things...

@1089. For the end selects the means, and applies them to itself; and means which are applied to the end, which is domination over the souls of men... cannot be truths...

