@DWis 8. 7. (A Spirit) takes with him from the inmost things of nature a medium between the Spiritual and the Natural, through which he is bounded, so as to be subsistent and permanent. Through this he has what is relative to the things which are in nature, and also what is correspondent to them. Through this also Spirits and Angels can be adjoined to and conjoined with the human race. For there is conjunction; and where there is conjunction there must also be a medium. That there is such a medium, the Angels know; but as it is from the inmost things of nature, and the words of languages are from its ultimates, it cannot be described except by abstract things.

