Medulla oblongata.; Medulla oblongata.

@AC 4325. The fibres (of the voluntary sense from the cerebrum, and of the involuntary sense from the cerebellum) conjoin themselves in the two appendices which are called the medulla oblongata and the medulla spinalis, and pass through them into the body, and form together its members, viscera, and organs.

